'''Robert James Holt''' (born October 4, 1959) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[wide receiver]] for the [[Buffalo Bills]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL) in 1982.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-buffalo-news/163634937/ | title=Turnover By Holt Is Costly | work=[[The Buffalo News]] | date=December 28, 1982 | accessdate=21 January 2025}}</ref> He played [[college football]] for the [[Baylor Bears football|Baylor Bears]] and was selected in the sixth round of the [[1981 NFL draft]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Robert Holt |url=https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/H/HoltRo20.htm |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221012122016/https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/H/HoltRo20.htm |archive-date=2022-10-12 |access-date=2023-04-16 |website=Pro-Football-Reference.com |language=en}}</ref>

As of 2022, Holt is a Physical Education Instructor at Gadsden Elementary in New Mexico.{{Citation needed|date=April 2023}}
